// app/Identity.xcconfig — the single tracked identity source of truth (D-45).
//
// Editing the four values below rebrands the app on both platforms. XcodeGen
// (configFiles:), Tuist (.settings(configurations:)) and xcodebuild all read
// this file natively — there is no parser in between, which is what lets
// `xcodebuild -showBuildSettings` report these resolved values directly.
// bin/preflight-identity.rb refuses to generate if any of the four is
// missing or empty, and names the variable (IDENT-09). The two keys after
// COPYRIGHT are a fifth slot and its helper — the privacy-policy URL the
// bundle carries — and are deliberately NOT in the IDENT-09 required set:
// a missing one is a missing link, not an unbranded app.
//
// Format rules: values are UNQUOTED (quotes would land in the plist as
// literal characters); comments are `//`; the `#` below is a directive, not
// a comment. `//` opens a comment ANYWHERE in a value, not only at the start
// of a line — which is why no URL below is written with a literal `//` in it.
// See the URL_SLASH comment at the bottom for the measurement.

// Feeds PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER on both app targets (one shared bundle id).
BUNDLE_ID        = com.indiagram.shipkitpipes.ios

// Feeds PRODUCT_NAME on the two APP targets only, through a per-target
// PRODUCT_NAME = $(APP_PRODUCT_NAME) in each manifest (D-49). Deliberately NOT
// a bare PRODUCT_NAME: a project-level PRODUCT_NAME leaks into every target —
// observed on Xcode 26.1.1, all four test bundles became ShipkitPipes.xctest
// and the two iOS ones collided at one path under
// Build/Products/Debug-iphonesimulator/. Tuist writes a per-target
// PRODUCT_NAME, so a bare one would also make the two generators disagree
// and fail the parity check. Do not simplify this back.
APP_PRODUCT_NAME = ShipkitPipes

// Feeds CFBundleDisplayName — the name under the icon — on both platforms.
DISPLAY_NAME     = Shipkit Pipes

// Feeds NSHumanReadableCopyright — the Info.plist key, set directly in both
// manifests' plist blocks — on both platforms. Not through an INFOPLIST_KEY_*
// build setting: that reaches the bundle only under GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE = YES,
// which the app targets do not set (observed: the setting resolved, the built
// iOS plist had no key). The organisation name matches the Apple enrollment
// name on record character for character (D-51, docs/APPLE-ACCOUNT-STATE.md).
// The © is U+00A9 — UTF-8 bytes c2 a9.
COPYRIGHT        = Copyright © 2026 Indiagram LLC. All rights reserved.

// Feeds the PrivacyPolicyURL Info.plist key — the URL the in-app privacy
// control opens, read by the app from its OWN bundle (D-120). Set directly in
// both manifests' plist blocks on both platforms, exactly as COPYRIGHT above
// is, and for the same reason: an INFOPLIST_KEY_* build setting reaches the
// bundle only under GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE = YES, which neither app target
// sets (observed: the setting resolved in -showBuildSettings, the built iOS
// plist had no key). PROJECT.md's parameterization constraint refuses a Swift
// or manifest literal, so the value crosses into the bundle only through this
// slot. UPSTREAM SHIPS THIS SLOT EMPTY — the generic mechanism goes to
// apple-shipkit, the fork-specific URL stays here (PROJECT.md:77).
//
// THE $(URL_SLASH) INDIRECTION IS MANDATORY AND IS NOT A STYLE CHOICE. `//` opens
// a comment at ANY position in an xcconfig value, so a plainly-written
// `= https://host/privacy/` is read as the four characters `https:` — by
// Xcode, not only by our parser. MEASURED 2026-09-11, Xcode 26.1.1, with
// `xcodebuild -showBuildSettings -project app/App.xcodeproj -target App-macOS
// -configuration Release -xcconfig <probe>`:
//
//     PROBE_PLAIN   = https://example.com/privacy/   ->  https:
//     PROBE_SLASHED = https:$(S)$(S)example.com/...  ->  https://example.com/privacy/
//
// The truncated form is the dangerous one: it is still a non-empty value with
// scheme `https`, so a presence check and a scheme check both pass on it while
// the shipped app opens nothing. URL_SLASH exists so no `//` is ever spelled
// on a value line. Do not "simplify" this back to a plain URL.
URL_SLASH        = /
PRIVACY_POLICY_URL = https:$(URL_SLASH)$(URL_SLASH)indiagrams.github.io/ios-macos-smoketest/privacy/

// The Apple Team ID (DEVELOPMENT_TEAM) lives in app/Local.xcconfig, which is
// gitignored under IDENT-08 and is never tracked. On a fresh clone the include
// below is silent and DEVELOPMENT_TEAM is undefined — not empty, undefined:
// no line for it appears in -showBuildSettings at all. The named failure comes
// from `bin/preflight-identity.rb --require-team`, not from the build (D-50).
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
